{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/98698-changelings-in-the-umbrae","id":98698,"title":"Changelings in the Umbrae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T15:07:51-07:00","id":98698,"title":"Changelings in the Umbrae","content":"I've poured through what books I have, and Googled a'plenty, but can't seem to find mention of how being in the Umbra/Umbrae/Umbral Realms affects changelings. Does the fae mien become prominent as it does while in the Dreaming? Are cantrips easier to cast away from the banal Autumn World (aside from being in a Weaver-dominant area, or gods-forbid, on her Web). I have my own thoughts (yes and yes) for what works with my own narratives (specifically a ship crewed by Etherites and nockers - let that idea sink in), but I am wondering if there has been anything &quot;canon&quot; printed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T17:06:33-07:00","id":98797,"title":"","content":"Changelings don't usually have a way to get to the Umbra unless they are Nunnehi or Menehune, in which case they go to the Umbra instead of the Dreaming, I think. As for Banality, the Changeling player's guide placed it as equal or very similar to the locale's Gauntlet, which never really decreases below 2. Beings, however, might have more or less. Wyldlings and Munchmausen Ratkin would be on the less side, while, as you note, weaver spirits would go higher. Garou and most other Fera of higher Rank probably also climb high in Banality, since they've seen some shit; also, the higher you climb in the spirit hierarchy, the more bound you are to it.<br /> <br /> Around heavy areas of Wyld taint, it might be lower. Around the other two members of the Triat, expect it to increase markedly, since Corruption is generally just as emptying in terms of Glamour as Stasis. Fomori, no matter what way you slice it, aren't very glamorous. Neither are the banes that produce them, or the Black Spiral Dancers that truck with them. It's all mindless indulgence this and violation that, without end.<br /> <br /> The Dark Umbra is probably going to be even bleaker than that, but given that it runs off of feelings, you could say that Banality = local Shroud. Don't hang around Nihils, though. Specters are roughly as glamorous as banes. Nunnehi can actually control ghosts with Spirit Link 5, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-25-2014, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T18:33:28-07:00","id":98841,"title":"","content":"Ack... &quot;Banality&quot; scores... *headache*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T02:22:36-07:00","id":109116,"title":"","content":"There isn't much about Changeling the Umbra outside the Nuneheii or Hisen. I always ran it that their Fae Meins became Wyrd while in the Umbra, and didn't bring up Banality unless they were dealing with the Weaver. The Umbra is a fantasical place and IMHO not all that Banal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T02:38:51-07:00","id":116867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/98698-changelings-in-the-umbrae?p=109116#post109116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't much about Changeling the Umbra outside the Nuneheii or Hisen. I always ran it that their Fae Meins became Wyrd while in the Umbra, and didn't bring up Banality unless they were dealing with the Weaver. The Umbra is a fantasical place and IMHO not all that Banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. The Dreaming is metaphysically separate from most Umbral Realities, but much/most of the Umbra is more dynamic/&quot;open&quot; than the general physical world, overall. (Btw: if one *has* to delineate the metaphysical &quot;location&quot; of The Dreaming, it exists in its own way -- as its own Umbral reality, so to speak -- &quot;between&quot; the Middle and High Umbrae, not entirely &quot;ephemeral matter&quot; -- Middle Umbra -- but also not wholly abstracted in nature -- High Umbra -- but somewhere in between.) While many aspects of the Low Umbra (particularly the upper levels, The Shadowlands) are &quot;compatible&quot; with some Fae aspects (the Slouagh, for example), due to certain emotional resonances, it's still relatively &quot;blargh&quot;/Banal for many/most Fae beings, despite existing off of emotion and (in a sense) certain qualities similar to Glamour, albeit in a &quot;negative&quot; state.<br /> <br /> But anywho...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}